    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549-a1">

                <pb facs="0974" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg878"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Buck</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1886</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 67</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 94 of the 24th ultimo,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d549-f1"/> intimating that new formal credentials to the
                    lately elected President of Peru, might withdraw the opportunity which
                    circumstances now seem to offer you, of being Dean of the Diplomatic Corps at
                    Lima, is received and the suggestion will be borne in mind. As a general thing
                    new credentials (maintaining the same rank) do not alter the precedence gained
                    by priority of original reception. This is the rule the United States follows.
                    We have already recognized the present Provisional Government of Peru, as in
                    transit toward a provisional constitutional Government.</p>
                <p>You will adopt whatever may be an acceptable form of recognition of the President
                    on his taking office. If new credentials should be needed, you will report the
                    fact, when they can be sent.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
